{"diagnosis": "Trace is minimal/unclear: only TRAP: cpu trap asserted and tohost FAIL 0xdead after CYCLES=2009 on 256-word NOP fetch test with no per-cycle PC/mem signals. mem_done is asserted early vs expected only on terminal mem_state with active rinst, causing mis-fetch and trap. Root cause in excerpt picorv32.v:376 uses (&mem_state || mem_do_rinst) instead of (&mem_state && mem_do_rinst).", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -375,3 +375,3 @@
 	wire mem_busy = |{mem_do_prefetch, mem_do_rinst, mem_do_rdata, mem_do_wdata};
-	wire mem_done = resetn && ((mem_xfer && |mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata || mem_do_wdata)) || (&mem_state || mem_do_rinst)) &&
+	wire mem_done = resetn && ((mem_xfer && |mem_state && (mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata || mem_do_wdata)) || (&mem_state && mem_do_rinst)) &&
 			(!mem_la_firstword || (~&mem_rdata_latched[1:0] && mem_xfer));
", "expected": "tohost PASS (not FAIL 0xdead), no TRAP: cpu trap asserted"}

